Findings
- F1 Major. The weeks w02 to w07 hold meta.status draft, so the week route answers 404 for them, and the clip files stay outside the media bucket until task 3.4 runs. The phase changed no meta.status, so the import itself is clean. The PM decided at 14:2x that w02 to w07 stay draft because Workbooks owns meta.status, and that look P3 gains the tasks 3.5 and 3.6 with a review-only switch STORYTIME_REVIEW_DRAFT_WEEKS=1 that opens draft weeks in the local review environment only. The fact is a planned task, not a blocker of this review.
- F2 Minor. The normalizer of the tap is toLowerCase only, so a future page word with a curly apostrophe or with trailing punctuation would be a visible tap target whose key lookup misses. The phase did not introduce the normalizer, and no imported word shows the gap today.
- F3 Minor. The w01 decodable book ships 11 clip keys that no screen plays. The decodable word tap still cuts the sentence recording. The phase introduced the data, and the decodable behaviour is pre-existing.

Browser review set-up
- The review opens the weeks with the review-only switch of the tasks 3.5 and 3.6, and it serves the clips from the media root of the hand-off folder, because the clip files are not in the media bucket until task 3.4 runs.
- The P3.8 line of each week reads own_clip. Every timed word of every book of w02 to w07 holds a clip, so the shipped data holds no word that has no clip. The review proves the second case with a fixture, or it records that the property holds for every word of the week.

Checks
- Focused tests through heavy-run, foreground: exit 0. Test Files 3 passed (3); Tests 27 passed (27); duration 7.79 s. The files are __tests__/look-word-clip-tap.test.tsx, __tests__/look-r3-import.test.ts and __tests__/look-adversarial-clips.test.tsx.
- bash measure/doctor.sh: exit 1. Two PASS lines and one FAIL line: FAIL: measure/automation-supervisor.py not found. That line is the known Nit. No other FAIL line appears, so the doctor does not block the phase.
- The file and line numbers of the tap words: measured with rg -n on the seven week files of the working tree, which hold the same content as the audited head.

Verdict
- Pass. The import keeps the child-facing contract, and the phase changed data only. No blocking finding and no violation list holds an item.
- F1 is a planned task after the PM decision of 14:2x, so no question goes to the user and the retry recommendation stays none.

